# The cases whose drawing is outside the tolerance of the reference and is nonetheless the correct one.
#
# The reference PNG is one oracle among several, so a case is correct, not merely close, when the
# behavior is undefined and the library's choice is documented, when the oracles disagree and the
# specification or the majority decides, or when the specification's text decides against the
# reference. A row says which, and gives the evidence. The row is reviewed one case at a time:
# there is no glob, and no bulk accept.
#
# <case> TAB <kind> TAB <evidence> TAB <reason> TAB <seen>
#
# The path is relative to the corpus's tests/ directory.
#
# kind      UNDEFINED     the specification leaves the behavior undefined, and the library's
#                         behavior is a documented choice (documentation/design.md)
#           DISAGREEMENT  the oracles disagree among themselves, and the evidence names which agree
#                         with the library and why those are the right ones
#           SPECIFICATION the text of the specification decides, and the reference differs from it
# evidence  what was observed: the oracles and what each did, from the corpus's results table or a
#           run of the oracle containers; a pointer to a section of the specification
# reason    why the library's drawing is the correct one, in a sentence a stranger can check
# seen      what the runner reports for the case (copied from the score's cases.tsv). The row is
#           refused if the case passes, is refused, or is drawn differently, so a row cannot go
#           stale without someone looking at it again.
#
# score.py fails on a row of any other shape, a case that is excluded, a glob, evidence or a reason
# of fewer than three words, and a case listed twice.
